  "body": "**This PR has scoped obstructions and a screening table. There is no new \u03ba, and the selected record is unchanged.**\n\n- Track: bit supplier, seed 3.\n- Card: `bit-helper-contract`, with the scope **changed**. The card question is saturated, and the register-model card is done in #1333.\n- Base: `bce54fb3`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe **proposed** priority revision 3 (open #1272, stacked on open #1240) prices the centre-path, rank-shape and coverage-law levers for the complex supplier only. This PR adds the bit-side numbers for the selected PR589 supplier.\n\n## Model and premises\n\nThe arithmetic uses exact rational intervals, standard library only, and imports no repository engine.\n\nIt is #1240's coverage-law relaxation, applied to the bit side:\n- Per call, the paid mass is (m\u2212u)w + cst, with m = 64, w = 888/9 and cst = 63. This gives D = W \u2212 63N, as in format-limits (Dfc).\n- Local children are either the replayed word or the most favorable in-window shapes: each data register is one rank-7 climb, and each helper is one climb whose rank equals its width.\n- Copies are carried at rank 7. This is a premise; at rank 8 nothing changes.\n- Idle mass goes to the halving-depth cap, with fractional counts and no surcharge. Each of these steps can only lower the bill, so a certified fail rules out every construction that meets the premises.\n\n**The idle cap is a premise tied to the halving depth.**\n- `global_k.py` raises the halving depth until 2\u00b7maxchild^HD < m^HD.\n- The row bound limits HD:\n  - The record uses HD 2 under the PR510 bound (row 18355), so the cap is 45.\n  - The merged elementary-cover bound (`row_bound.py`) admits HD \u2264 4, which gives caps 50 and 53.\n- Results are reported at caps 45, 50 and 53. Cap 63 is a robustness bound only.\n\n## Results (certified at a = 1/99)\n\n| Bit lever (cap 45) | root a | \u00d7 | 1/99 |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| Packing ceiling (reproduces merged #1023's free concentration) | 0.0019559 | 1 | fail |\n| Centre path free | 0.0054196 | 2.771 | fail |\n| Centre path shared by two calls | 0.0036864 | 1.885 | fail |\n| Two unpaid coordinates | 0.0073120 | 3.738 | fail |\n| Rank-8 children / rank-16 children | 0.0032114 / 0.0047309 | 1.642 / 2.419 | fail |\n| Centre free + rank-8 (shipped helper mass) | 0.0089383 | 4.570 | fail |\n| Centre free + rank-16 / + two unpaid | 0.0131671 / 0.0107587 | 6.732 / 5.501 | pass |\n| Centre free + ideal data + \u2264 332 width-8 helpers (in window) | 0.0101021 | 5.165 | pass |\n| Two unpaid + ideal in-window shapes (copies kept) | 0.0117941 | 6.030 | pass |\n\nThe fail rows also fail at caps 50, 53 and 63.\n\n**O1 (copy charge 63).**\n- Even with no helpers and ideal data, the bill exceeds 1 at a = 1/99 at every cap from 42 to 63.\n- The ceiling is 0.006794 at cap 45 and 0.009665 at cap 63.\n\n**O2 (centre path shared, copy charge 31.5, full-frame width-8 helpers).**\n- The maximum helper count is 104, 131 and 145 at caps 45, 50 and 53. Each count k is certified: k passes and k+1 fails.\n- The strict design-free floor of format-limits section D is 138. It applies to full-frame helpers and is cited as an argued premise.\n- **The obstruction holds at halving depth \u2264 3 and flips at depth 4.**\n\n**Joint surface.** The README has the table of copy charge \u00d7 full-frame helper count at caps 45, 50 and 53, for ideal and shipped data shapes.\n\n**What it does not say.**\n- With the shipped helper mass, centre free needs rank-16 children or a second unpaid coordinate.\n- But in this relaxation, fewer helpers (\u2264 332) or a second unpaid coordinate reach 1/99 *inside* today's windows.\n\n**Complex side.**\n- #1240's ceiling is reproduced.\n- #1272's \u00d76.5 combination (0.011008) needs rank-16 children beyond the window h = 9.\n- Inside the window, centre free + rank-9 gives 0.008128 (fail), and two unpaid + rank-9 gives 0.010911 (pass).\n\n## Checks\n\n- **Bindings.** Selected record \u2192 frontier1094 certificate \u2192 `PR589-EXPECTED.json` \u2192 bit word, endpoint, halving depth and row coefficient. The row-bound and halving-depth source lines are pinned.\n- **Positive controls.** The selected bit endpoint is accepted and the next 1e-24 point is rejected, with the surcharge. #1240's complex ceiling is reproduced.\n- **Replay.** The local histogram equals the record: mass 5,129 and the class split. The profile equals 288 local words plus idle.\n- **Tests (15).** They cover:\n  - the interval engine and the endpoint;\n  - the relaxation steps;\n  - the guards and the halving-depth cap table;\n  - the O1 and O2 boundaries at each cap;\n  - the in-window centre-free boundary (332 passes, 333 fails);\n  - tampering.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/bit-revision3-levers-seed03/verify.py           # ~13 s; PASS_BIT_REVISION3_LEVERS\npython3 -I -B -m unittest discover -s research/bit-revision3-levers-seed03 -p test_package.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/bit-revision3-levers-seed03\n```\n\n## Overlap\n\n- #1240 and #1272 (Douglas Colkitt / Mister-Meeseeks): this is the bit analogue, in independent code.\n- #1293 (navinor): reconciled in the README.\n- Merged format-limits sections A, A.4, A.7 and D. A.7's \u00d72.79 cross-checks the centre-free row.\n- #974 (avirazza).\n- #1023 (ours, merged): the packing ceiling is reproduced, not claimed as new.\n- #1281 (mightyOil).\n- #1194, #1311, #1179, #1253 and #1128.\n- #1333 / #1317 (bitplane).\n\n## Disclosure\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar (thakrarsagar) with substantial AI assistance from Claude (Anthropic) via Claude Code. Parallel read-only scout and judge subagents ranked the question. A post-PR adversarial review found the halving-depth error and two overclaims; all are corrected in the second commit. No claim was posted to Discussions. Apache-2.0.\n",
